WEBVTT

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.980
I recall asking you for something that <i>didn't</i> sting.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.900
Would you prefer one that stung even more?

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.020
You mean this is better than most?

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.040
Paint, paint...

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.270
Okay, I'm done.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.640
Master...

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.280
We have come to get you.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.070
Got it.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.460
I'll be back.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.290
Oh, Haku...

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.610
Yeah, what is it?

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.790
Um... be back by dinnertime, okay?

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.170
Sure thing.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.060
This isn't much fun...

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:37.480
I heard you made quite a name for 
yourself in the war with the Uzuurussha.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.590
I received a report from Oshutoru.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:41.470
Huh?

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.480
Oh, everyone else did all the work.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.040
I didn't do anything.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:50.550
The glories of the soldiers are 
the glories of the general.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.300
They're not my soldiers.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.390
They're...

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.260
like family, I guess.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.600
Family, you say?

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.310
Did you need to go that far?

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.610
"That far"?

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.620
In the war with the Uzuurussha.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.190
The power of those masks...

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.290
You must've been terrified, I'm sure.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.800
But that terror is necessary.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.350
No one is immune to the terror of destruction.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:42.280
Thus they attempt to flee,
to distance themselves from it.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.810
That is the way of all living creatures.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.690
That's why you did all that?

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.820
To teach them what happens 
if they oppose Yamato?

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.820
What is the task of an emperor, if not to protect his people?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.650
I see.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.790
But terror fades, eventually.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:08.440
This was not the first Uzuurussha invasion.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.270
The previous one was...

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.490
Two hundred years ago, I believe.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.420
Two <i>hundred</i> years!?

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.090
Just how old are you?

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.350
Perhaps it's time.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:24.900
Yes.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.350
Follow me.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:40.360
This world was once ruled by the 
Great Forefathers, the Onvitaikayan,

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.370
who possessed a highly advanced civilization.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.750
The Onvitaikayan?

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.440
With their power, they created the people,

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.680
and then vanished, leaving no 
trace of themselves behind.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.290
The people they left behind built 
nations on this land and flourished.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.760
That is how this world began.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:06.560
Most people in this world possess ears and tails not unlike those of animals.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.270
But there are those who do not:

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.770
you, and I.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.780
You must have found it strange...

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.610
Why you were different from them.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.870
The answer lies ahead.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:28.050
Do you wish to know?

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.710
Why are you telling me?

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:34.040
Open!

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.590
Come with me.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:47.520
Are you sure about this?

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.140
Huh?

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:51.180
You can still go back.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:52.770
Honoka-san...

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:18.190
Very good.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:20.590
You haven't changed.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:58.710
The environment is 85% restored.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.420
Amaterasu's sure working hard,

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:06.890
but we haven't managed to adapt yet.
What's up with that?

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:10.360
If you think so, then why not help?

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:14.480
The director of the afforestation 
plant spoke very highly of you.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.400
The problem is the topic of their research.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.190
Making daikon radishes that run?

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.180
What's the point of that? To make them race?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:21.540
Hey, you never know!

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.560
Then how about you come help with my research?

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.200
You know I wouldn't be able to help.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:32.170
You have a bad habit of underestimating yourself.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.130
Fine. Tell me if you change your mind.

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.120
Sure.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.860
Also, try adjusting your camera.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:41.210
I can't see your face.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:41.960
Oh, sure.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:50.980
Hey, Sis.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.970
You're still just eating rations.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.390
You need to eat some real food.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.150
It's convenient, you know.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.420
<i>Men</i>. We take our eyes off you for a minute and look what happens.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.070
You're as bad as my husband.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.680
You don't have to do that.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.260
It's fine.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.240
What are you doing?

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.270
Nothing much.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.220
Oh, yeah!

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:32.150
Good news, Uncle! 
I'm making curry today, your favorite!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.600
Good! Make it as spicy as you can, okay?

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:36.290
Sure!

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.130
I can't believe you got this far in.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:43.670
Hey, you're the one who told me to do it.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:46.530
They're up to some pretty dicey stuff.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:52.050
They're using the genes from the 
ancient human they found in a coma

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:55.160
to engineer people capable of 
surviving on the surface.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.610
The Iceman Project.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.670
How arrogant are they going to get?

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.550
They fear destruction and try to flee it.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:08.920
None can defy the instincts of their species.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:15.050
Hey, Uncle!

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:21.940
I'm not old enough to be your uncle, you know.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:25.330
Call me Big Brother.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:29.490
But you're my daddy's little brother, 
so you're my uncle,

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:30.740
Uncle!

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:37.700
Mommy, Uncle's being mean!

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.700
Oh, my.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:45.770
Listen, boys can't help teasing the girls they love,

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.120
so it's a good woman's job to forgive them.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:50.100
Okay!

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:53.150
I'm a good woman, so I'll forgive him.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.030
Don't teach her anything too weird.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:02.180
I can't wait to go outside.

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.910
Me too.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:06.920
I hear your daddy is working very hard.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:07.990
Good!

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.420
Uncle, did you know?

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.990
When you eat curry outside, 
it's called "camping"!

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:24.270
That's right.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.250
Well, not <i>exactly</i>, but...

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:31.500
If it works, let's all go camping! 
You and Mommy and Daddy and me!

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.390
Yes.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:33.590
I can't wait.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:43.480
Now here's a face we don't usually see here.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.000
I've got nothing else to do.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.960
So I thought I'd take a look at your research.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:56.990
Looks like you're strengthening and enhancing the 
fundamental capabilities of the body?

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.890
If this works, not only will we
adapt to the environment,

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.130
we'll overcome genetic diseases, too.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:05.730
Lifespans will also increase drastically.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:09.840
And that's your True Human Project?

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.610
All that's left is the final test?

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:17.530
It's tough finding a test 
subject in this environment.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.670
Well, I guess there's always me.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.330
Hey, could I do it?

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.110
You're sure about this?

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:37.360
Well, I have to do this, don't I?

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.290
Thanks. This is a huge help.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.450
I love you, Big Brother.

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:44.830
I love you too, Little Brother.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:51.390
Stop screwing around and get started already!

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.420
You're the one who made me do it!

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:57.730
I'm starting.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:11:59.520
Right...

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:26.150
How do you feel?

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.710
What was that?

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:32.990
The Onvitaikayan...

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.790
The ones we call the Great Forefathers.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:41.220
They once had another name.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:43.970
"Human beings."

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:47.620
Yes.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:51.200
That is what we are.

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:56.750
What happened to the humans 
after they vanished?

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.620
They did not disappear,

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:00.750
nor did they go extinct.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:05.240
Though perhaps it would've been better if they had.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.250
What do you mean?

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:11.250
This is what the average
human being looks like now.

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:14.750
The curse!

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:20.090
Yes. Humans are simultaneously 
revered as the Onvitaikayan,

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:23.250
and hated and feared as the curses.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.770
How ironic.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.770
Why?

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.390
The Calamity.{we bastion now}

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:40.210
That day, humans suddenly started to melt.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:43.920
We knew neither the cause, nor how to stop it.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.480
All we could do was quake 
in fear in our shelters.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.490
But that was only the beginning.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:58.960
Once they melted, they attacked others.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.470
When would you start to melt yourself?

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:09.490
When would your family, your friends,
and your neighbors attack you?

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:13.160
The world was consumed by insecurity and fear,

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.520
and everyone became the enemy.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:23.740
War begets war.

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:27.020
Humans distrusted each other,

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:28.180
feared each other,

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:29.740
and killed each other.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:37.400
And then, we made the
most foolish choice we could.

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:23.510
In the aftermath of the destruction,

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:29.800
naught remained but the decoys we 
once created for use in experiments.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.680
Such was the fate of the human race.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:39.680
Luckily, or perhaps unluckily...

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:43.320
the Calamity did not befall me.

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:49.510
This was the beginning of a long, long journey.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.780
For what seemed like an eternity, I'd dreamed of the surface,

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.640
and yet getting there was so easy.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:13.790
Perhaps the great destruction had 
changed Earth's environment,

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:19.400
or perhaps my own body had
adapted to it. I can't say.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.630
But there was nothing there.

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:28.930
Not my wife, nor my child, 
nor my little brother...

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:33.310
I had no one to share my joy with.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:40.000
I was left all alone in this world.

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:47.010
And I was unable to bear that loneliness.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:51.770
So I created decoys.

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:56.580
I gave them letters, numbers...

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:59.350
I gave them many things.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.330
It was enjoyable

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:07.010
to watch them begin as innocents 
and grow wiser by the day.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:10.430
They multiplied. They flourished.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:13.610
They grew as the human race once did.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:18.430
But even as they approached the level of mankind,

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.040
I realized...

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:25.230
They were not human.

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:30.150
No matter how much the decoys worshiped me,

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.820
it would not fulfill my heart's longing.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:37.560
And then they found a ruin...

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.020
An old research lab.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.560
If I brought back all that 
lost technology and knowledge,

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:49.230
perhaps I could revert the 
curses back into humans.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:52.370
I searched through all the ruins in the country

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:54.990
and dedicated myself to many 
different forms of research.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:59.310
I spent a long, long time at the task.

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:02.980
It was all I had...

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:05.110
Even if I knew it was impossible.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:07.350
But...

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:14.280
At last, I found family.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:18.340
Family? What do you...

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.880
You have a fine mind,

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:25.870
but you avoid looking at 
things you don't want to see.

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.890
It's a bad habit of yours.

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.910
You know, don't you?

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.130
Brother... Is that you?

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:43.890
It's been a long time.

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:53.210
My wife and daughter became 
curses before very my eyes.

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:57.010
Then Honoka-san and Anju...

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:01.520
Decoys made to their likeness.

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:05.080
Brother, you went that far?

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:11.530
I was willing to do whatever
it took to escape that hell.

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:15.970
Now, finally...

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:20.910
someone can carry on my hopes.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:26.150
Let's make up for the 
time we lost as a family.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.690
Welcome back, Haku.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.580
You must be hungry, right?

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:40.260
Help yourself.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:41.470
Sure.

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:50.020
Huh? You're not hungry?

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.760
Oh, that's not it...

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.030
Hey, Kuon...

00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:05.290
What do you think family is?

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:07.030
Huh?

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.290
Let me see...

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.340
Kind but strict,

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:16.110
sometimes annoying,

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:19.210
and I wish they'd stop being so clingy.

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:22.000
They always treat me like I'm a kid,

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.850
but then they insist that I act like an adult.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:27.060
Basically, a lot of trouble.

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:29.940
Come on...

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:31.080
But still...

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:36.530
All that trouble makes me feel 
happier and warmer than I can say.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:44.290
That was kind of embarrassing!

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:45.870
Forget it! Forget it!

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:52.000
Happier and warmer than you can say, huh?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.740
I told you to forget it!

00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:55.500
Sheesh!

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:01.110
Hey, didn't you make those for me?

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:02.510
I don't care!

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:05.540
I'm sorry, okay? I'm sorry, Kuon!

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:18.780
You're not going to sleep?

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:20.470
Nah.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.810
If you stay up all night,
you won't grow up big and strong.

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:25.660
I'm not a kid, you know.

00:21:26.270 --> 00:21:28.660
But I <i>am</i> your guardian.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.420
That's right.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:55.920
It flows beyond the horizon and disappears...

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:55.920
chihei no kanata e to nagare kieru

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:55.920
What's that song?

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:02.550
My mother sang it to me when I had trouble sleeping.

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:05.440
I see.

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:20.310
Quietly, a world without color comes,

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:20.310
shizuka ni otozureru iro naki sekai

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:34.060
and all time stops as I fall asleep...

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:34.060
subete no toki wo tome nemuri ni tsuku

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:43.930
Is it still not possible to grant us the location of the last Ouro's tomb?

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:56.610
He has at last come to rest 
after a long, violent journey.

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:03.550
All who live in Tusukuru pray 
for his peaceful slumber.

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:11.750
We humbly ask the Emperor of Yamato for forgiveness.

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:15.090
I understand.

00:23:15.090 --> 00:23:18.360
I shall relay every word to him.

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:19.190
Farewell.
